cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OSCR or its catalogue, please cite it as below."
title: "OSCR: Open Scientific Code Registry"
type: software
abstract: >-
  OSCR finds where the authors of open-access neuroscience papers published their
  code, verifies that code at the source (git, Zenodo, OSF, figshare, Software
  Heritage), keeps the text of the scripts, and pairs paragraphs of the paper with
  the lines of code that match them. The catalogue is released under CC0-1.0;
  tracing maps validated by one of a paper's authors receive a Zenodo DOI.
authors:
  - name: "The OSCR contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yannbellec/Open-Scientific-Code-Registry-OSCR-"
url: "https://oscr.yannbellec-b.workers.dev"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - research software
  - reproducibility
  - open science
  - neuroscience
  - code availability
  - software citation
  - scholarly infrastructure
  - Europe PMC
  - Zenodo
  - Software Heritage
